  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Trying to load a video on Android fails if the URL starts with HTTP rather than HTTPS.   I can understand that there's probably some technical reason why HTTP requests must be refused, but rather than silently failing, why not switch to HTTPS automatically?   (Of course some servers can't serve it, but if the original request is guaranteed to fail *anyway*, you could at least take a chance of success before giving up.)",
